WEBVTT

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:07.240
Everything on this table goes into
making one Array lampshade.

00:00:07.240 --> 00:00:12.900
I designed it, developed it into a
finished project and I already sell it.

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:18.840
You can make this and you can sell it
using just the tools here and a

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:21.700
Bambu Lab A1 printer.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:27.290
But making each one still involves too
much cutting, gluing and finishing

00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:28.390
by hand.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.500
Because it's too large for my build
plate, I need to print it out in

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:36.020
sections and glue them together.

00:00:36.233 --> 00:00:40.153
It gets the job done, but there's a lot
of work between the printer and

00:00:40.153 --> 00:00:42.373
the finished part.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:49.750
My funding goal is 3,000 euros to fund a
Bambu Lab H2D printer with laser

00:00:49.750 --> 00:00:51.490
cutting abilities.

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:55.980
I want to develop the project around
that machine, optimize the printed

00:00:55.980 --> 00:01:02.680
part and work towards printing this
ring in a single piece and test

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:07.400
repeatable workflow for cutting these slats.

00:01:07.990 --> 00:01:13.010
I want to spend less time trimming and
gluing the finished lamp and make

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:16.290
it easier for people to produce it.

00:01:16.840 --> 00:01:21.060
In return, you will get the project,
the improvements developed through

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:26.580
the campaign, and a license to make
and sell this under your own name.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:32.430
Now I want to make it even easier to
produce and even more flexible.
